  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_012 (acc=0.635, F1=0.618) using multiprofile + pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. The only major untested dimension within this winning recipe is the RNA encoder: all top configs use PCA (a linear projection), and it is unclear whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) could capture richer cell-state structure and push accuracy higher. config_027 isolates exactly that change—swapping pca_n2000 for scvi_n200 while keeping the proven multiprofile/avgpool/weighted/ViT-L backbone—so any accuracy gain or loss can be attributed to the RNA representation. This is a high-value exploitation step: if scvi helps, we get a new best config; if it doesn't, we confirm PCA is sufficient and can focus remaining budget on other axes (e.g., scgpt or image-only baselines). Expected cost is moderate, roughly 6–8 GPU hours, comparable to config_012's 7.02 h since the architecture and image encoder are identical and scvi_n200 is a compact VAE."
}

